{"team":"BAL","col":"#9E86FF","identity":"run-heavy","funnel":"pass-funnel","plays_pg":59.0,"adot":8.5,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Built to Run</h2><p>The backfield runs through one man \u2014 <strong>Derrick Henry</strong> absorbs <strong>76% of the carries</strong> (league ~59%), a true bell-cow share that makes his rushing volume among the safest floors in the sport when the script cooperates.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>Run identity is the through-line here: BAL call pass on <strong>-8%</strong> of snaps relative to what the situation expects (league -2%), and when they get ahead they lean even harder on the ground \u2014 just 30% pass on early downs with a lead. This is a ball-control operation built to shorten games.</p><p>Their run game attacks the perimeter \u2014 <strong>33% of carries hit the edge</strong> (league ~25%), an outside-zone lean that rewards speed backs and can boom for chunk gains.</p><p>By the numbers it's an efficient unit \u2014 a 48% success rate (above the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they lean run-heavy, passing <strong>43%</strong> of the time, funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>Derrick Henry</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 Stout Up Front, Soft in Coverage</h2><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR1s</strong> \u2014 74 rec yds/game (vs ~58). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They surrender <strong>94 rushing</strong> and <strong>257 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). They wall the run and force the throw \u2014 <strong>attack with the opposing WR room</strong>.</p><p><strong>Soft against backs out of the backfield</strong> \u2014 22 rec yds/game (vs ~18). A rec-yards target.</p><p>A stingy, efficient defense \u2014 just 42% success allowed (vs ~44%); temper expectations for opposing skill players.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: back <strong>Derrick Henry</strong>'s rushing volume in favored/positive scripts; <strong>opposing WR1/WR2</strong> are the target \u2014 this D forces the throw.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Lamar Jackson","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":11,"props":{"Comp":16.55,"Att":25.45,"Pass Yds":205.18,"Pass TD":1.57,"INT":1.29,"Rush Yds":16.02}}],"RB":[{"name":"Derrick Henry","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":47,"props":{"Rush Att":15.32,"Rush Yds":75.03,"Tgt":1.63,"Rec":1.3,"Rec Yds":12.36}},{"name":"Justice Hill","slot":"RB2","starter":true,"td":13,"props":{"Rush Att":1.4,"Rush Yds":6.52,"Tgt":2.25,"Rec":1.54,"Rec Yds":11.74}},{"name":"Adam Randall","slot":"RB4","starter":false,"td":12,"props":{"Rush Att":2.42,"Rush Yds":10.54,"Tgt":0.77,"Rec":0.52,"Rec Yds":3.44}}],"WR":[{"name":"Zay Flowers","slot":"WR1","starter":true,"td":23,"props":{"Tgt":6.0,"Rec":4.19,"Rec Yds":54.88,"Rec TD":0.25}},{"name":"Rashod Bateman","slot":"WR2","starter":true,"td":16,"props":{"Tgt":2.76,"Rec":1.71,"Rec Yds":22.65,"Rec TD":0.17}},{"name":"Ja'Kobi Lane","slot":"WR3","starter":true,"td":10,"props":{"Tgt":2.33,"Rec":1.27,"Rec Yds":15.72,"Rec TD":0.1}},{"name":"Devontez Walker","slot":"WR4","starter":false,"td":18,"props":{"Tgt":2.27,"Rec":1.25,"Rec Yds":17.92,"Rec TD":0.2}},{"name":"Elijah Sarratt","slot":"WR5","starter":false,"td":11,"props":{"Tgt":2.37,"Rec":1.3,"Rec Yds":16.05,"Rec TD":0.11}}],"TE":[{"name":"Mark Andrews","slot":"TE1","starter":true,"td":22,"props":{"Tgt":3.49,"Rec":2.49,"Rec Yds":28.93,"Rec TD":0.25}},{"name":"Durham Smythe","slot":"TE2","starter":false,"td":4,"props":{"Tgt":1.8,"Rec":1.15,"Rec Yds":10.72,"Rec TD":0.04}},{"name":"Matthew Hibner","slot":"TE3","starter":false,"td":12,"props":{"Tgt":2.41,"Rec":1.46,"Rec Yds":14.85,"Rec TD":0.12}}]},"schedule":[{"week":1,"ha":"@","opp":"IND","opp_col":"#4F9BE8","gid":"2026_01_BAL_IND","spread":"\u22123.5","proj":"26\u201323","win":true},{"week":2,"ha":"vs","opp":"NO","opp_col":"#D9BE72","gid":"2026_02_NO_BAL","sp